it's a great time to be a sci-fi fan but  which films should you be watching  the past year gave us an onslaught of  mind-bending adventures  to choose from so without further ado  here are the best sci-fi movies of 2020.  canadian author filmmaker david  cronenberg has masterfully merged horror  and sci-fi themes on numerous occasions  throughout his career  and his son brandon cronenberg managed  the same feat with 2020's possessor  the film was met with rave reviews  earning widespread praise from the  critics  possessor is the story of tarzia played  by mandy's andrea rysborough an agent of  a corporation that uses brain implant  tech  to take control of people victims are  turned into unwilling hitmen  carrying out assassinations ordered by  the company's rich and powerful clients  tarzia is a natural at the job but she  gets more than she bargained for when  she inhabits the body of a man who  serves to violence eclipses even her own  the experienced agent loses control of  her host mind  and finds herself in danger of never  being able to escape it  leading to a thrilling and highly  abstract showdown between possessor and  host  [Music]  if any one movie was going to coax  people back into theaters in 2020 it was  tenet  christopher nolan's 11th feature was the  first blockbuster to play in theaters  during the coronavirus pandemic and it  certainly helped people take their minds  off covet 19 for a while  john david washington starts as a former  cia agent who's been recruited by a  secret organization  tenet which is working to prevent world  war iii he learns that weapons with  inverted entropy  manufactured in the future are somehow  making their way to the present day and  things get a whole lot weirder from  there  with help from robert pattinson's neil  washington's unnamed protagonist  learns that a russian oligarch has been  in contact with the future  our descendants have grown tired of the  ravaged world left of them and they  intend to invert the flow of time  in a last-ditch effort to change the  world it may not be christopher nolan's  finest film  but the slick action sequences and  impeccable performances make tennis one  of 2020s must-see  sci-fi films if an homage to ridley  scott's aliens said drawing the height  of the cold war  sounds like something you'd be  interested in you need to check out  sputnik  this slick russian creature feature was  forced to forego a theatrical release  because of the coronavirus pandemic  but it found lots of love on vod in its  native country  genre film distributor ifc midnight  secured the release rights for north  america  where critics have been raving about  igor abramenko's stylish debut  on paper abramenko's story is nothing  groundbreaking but he executes his scary  alien vision superbly  sputnik follows a cosmonaut who gets  quarantined after his vessel  malfunctions re-entering the earth's  atmosphere  what he doesn't know is that there's an  extraterrestrial parasite living inside  him  and when he sleeps it comes out to feed  the russian military manages to keep  this a secret  hoping to separate the creature from its  host and use it as a weapon of war  the cosmonauts only hope is a  sympathetic neurophysiologist who begins  masterminding his escape with suspense  to spare sputnik is a white knuckle  thrill ride that you can't afford to  miss  sci-fi comedy save yourselves is a story  of a young brooklyn couple  who decide to disconnect from the modern  world for a while they head out into  rural new york without their phones or  devices  while they're away aliens invade earth  and our heroes have absolutely no idea  as cities across america are reduced to  rubble our heroes busy themselves with  unbusying themselves  the city dwellers take advantage of the  nearby lake and surrounding nature  blissfully unaware that humankind is  under attack from fluffy but extremely  vicious extraterrestrials  gradually they come to the realization  that something isn't quite right  and their millennial morals are tested  when they discover a gun in the cabin's  basement  when push comes to shove they would  rather bear arms and be killed by a ball  of space fluff  writer directors alex huston fisher and  eleanor wilson didn't have a huge budget  so the majority of the action including  the levelling of yankee stadium  happens off screen this isn't a big vfx  heavy sci-fi film  but it really doesn't need to be sunita  mani and john paul reynolds are both  funny and convincing are sue and jack  and their vacation turned survival  mission is engaging enough that we don't  need to seal the peripheral destruction  we need to turn our phones back on  [Applause]  sorry making a smoothie listen it's  getting weird here in new york  bill and ted face the music was a tonic  for trying times in 2020.  alex winters bill s preston esquire and  keanu reeves ted theodore logan  returned to the big screen for a belated  third adventure in late summer  though the coronavirus pandemic meant it  had an unusual theatrical release  box office returns were a predictably  dire 3.3 million dollars  but bill and ted face the music was also  released on pvod  and deadline sources suggest it made  around 10 times that amount via  streaming in the same period  the simultaneous release meant critics  nationwide got to see the movie  and the majority of them deemed it most  excellent our titular besties are now  middle-aged fathers  as bill and ted go forward in time in  search of their future selves  their daughters go in the opposite  direction recruiting iconic musicians  for the band that will help their dads  finally perform their universe  saving song reeves and winter slip back  into their roles with ease  and their on-screen daughters are just  as watchable variety called the film a  blissed-out air balloon of nostalgia in  a glowing review  while the hollywood reporter called it  quote almost exactly as good as its two  big screen predecessors  archive may not win any awards for  originality but as the hollywood  reporter puts it  the directorial debut of concept artist  gavin rothery is a quote sleek and  satisfying riff on familiar sci-fi  themes  rothery's film plays like a mashup of ex  machina and black mirror  and takes place in 2038 when a widowed  roboticist named george almore is on the  verge of a groundbreaking advancement  almor works for a mega corporation that  specializes in artificial intelligence  when we meet him his human equivalent  prototype is just about ready  but this isn't just a replication of any  old human the savvy scientist has  recreated his deceased wife  in robot ai form behind the backs of his  bosses the trouble is his creation ends  up being a little too real  we're not going to spoil it here but  trust us when we say the archive  contains one of the best movie twists  of 2020 sci-fi or otherwise  sci-fi adventure love and monsters  proved popular when it was released on  pvod in october 2020  and the critics loved it too this  dystopian teen film takes place some  seven years after mankind  turned its nukes on a planet-killing  asteroid that was on a collision course  with earth  they destroyed their intended target but  nobody was quite prepared for the brutal  aftermath the fallout caused all  cold-blooded animals to mutate into huge  terrifying creatures  former maze runner star dylan o'brien  leaves the line as one of a number of  survivors  living in an underground bunker the film  was lauded as an imaginative  post-apocalyptic coming-of-age film  by the new york times while variety  called it a quote  definitely lightweight throwback to the  teen action adventures of the 80s and  90s  marvel fans will recognize some familiar  faces here joel's girlfriend amy is  played by iron fist star jessica henwick  michael rooker of guardians of the  galaxy and ariana greenblatt from  avengers infinity war  also make appearances in the film  spontaneous was one of the most  critically acclaimed movies of 2020  scoring a near perfect 98 on rotten  tomatoes  in brian duffield's directorial debut  students at covington high school have  started to inexplicably explode at  random intervals  sowing dread and anxiety among their  surviving classmates  the film's quarantined scenes drew  inevitable comparisons to the  coronavirus pandemic but spontaneous was  done and dusted before covid19 was a  thing  according to deathfield his goal was to  make a movie that captured what it meant  to be a kid  at that moment in time he said in his  looper exclusive interview  i'm very liberal and for me the movie  feels like a very real thing that kids  are dealing with right now  when we shot the movie there were these  things happening in the world where it  really felt like kids were being like we  need someone to help us  and it was really falling on deaf ears  the writer director also revealed that  80's classic heathers and the films of  john hughes were among his many  inspirations  fifty shades of greystar jamie dornan  and avengers actor anthony mackie  play a pair of paramedics in synchronic  a new orleans set sci-fi that made a big  impression when it premiered at the  toronto international film festival  directed by justin benson and aaron  morehead synchronic follows dennis and  steve as they're called to a series of  strange and gruesome incidents  the pair believes that a new designer  drug called synchronic is to blame for  it all  but when dennis's daughter seriously  goes missing it's up to steve to  investigate further  he soon discovers that synchronic is  more than meets the eye these mysterious  pills allow the user to travel through  time  one of the many criticisms leveled at  the fifty shades franchise was that the  coast stars had zero chemistry  but that certainly isn't a problem here  dornan and mackie sold their  relationship  well delivering believable performances  as two best friends going through  personal ruts  synchronic gets pretty trippy but the  two leads keep us invested in their  modern day problems  check out one of our newest videos right  here plus even more looper videos about  your favorite new movies are coming soon  subscribe to our youtube channel and hit  the bell so you don't miss a single one
 

